WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
An early nun sits in meditation.

2
00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:05.920
Mara, the tempter, taunts her.

3
00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:09.370
A woman, he says, has
only two-finger wisdom.

4
00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:11.760
She can never reach the goal.

5
00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:16.210
Over the centuries, Buddhist texts
go on telling stories about women,

6
00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:18.360
wisdom and the goal.

7
00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:20.900
So can a woman become a Buddha?

8
00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:24.130
And why do Buddhist texts
give different answers?

9
00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:28.530
In this mission, you'll read what the
earliest texts say about women and the goal

10
00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:29.750
of the path.

11
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:33.380
Then you'll weigh up whether
Buddhism is feminist at its core,

12
00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:35.540
with the scholar Rita Gross.

13
00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:39.200
Your mission: find out whether
a woman can become a Buddha,

14
00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:41.170
and why the texts disagree.
